# Visual Studio 2022 (17.8+) HTTP file. Open it and click "Send request" above a request (or press Ctrl+Alt+S inside it).
# Start Mobile.Gateway (API 1, port 5090) and Mobile.DataApi (API 2, port 5091) first.
# Do NOT commit real passwords or keys in this file.
#
# THE FLOW
#   1st time : call API 1 (request 1) with the company login, password and API key -> you get "appConfig". The app SAVES it as its
#              config file: API 2 address + end points, company details and the access token. No database connection is in it.
#   from then: the app reads its file and calls ONLY API 2 with  Authorization: Bearer <appConfig.auth.token>  (requests 2-5).
#              The device is validated by API 2 (request 5). API 1 is called again by the app itself when refreshAfter is reached.

@api1 = http://localhost:5090
@api2 = http://localhost:5091

# The company's details (from MobileKeyManager); deviceId is the phone's id, checked by API 2.
@username = <company login>
@password = <company password>
@apikey = <company API key>
@appUser = <app user name>
@deviceId = TEST1

### 0. Health check (API 1)
GET {{api1}}/health

### 1. FIRST TIME: sign in through API 1 and get appConfig
# @name provision
POST {{api1}}/gateway/v1/provision
x-username: {{username}}
x-password: {{password}}
x-api-key: {{apikey}}

### 2. From now on only API 2: the masters this company's database says to read, in order (send request 1 first)
GET {{api2}}/mobile/v1/plan
Authorization: Bearer {{provision.response.body.$.appConfig.auth.token}}

### 3. Read a master from the company's own database
GET {{api2}}/mobile/v1/masters/division
Authorization: Bearer {{provision.response.body.$.appConfig.auth.token}}

### 4. Another master
GET {{api2}}/mobile/v1/masters/tea-estate
Authorization: Bearer {{provision.response.body.$.appConfig.auth.token}}

### 5. Device check (the app user's registered device, in the customer's database)
GET {{api2}}/mobile/v1/auth/device-check?username={{appUser}}&deviceId={{deviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{provision.response.body.$.appConfig.auth.token}}
x-app-user: {{appUser}}
